  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current Pollution Under Control (PUC) Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid PUC certificate proves that the vehicle meets emission standards. The certificate should be issued within the last 90 days and must be presented alongside the RC copy to avoid delays at port or customs checkpoints.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Prior to loading, obtain a comprehensive insurance certificate that covers physical damage, theft, and third‑party liability. This certificate should be issued by a licensed insurer and explicitly state the policy number, coverage period, and claim contact details.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The International Bilty Association (IBA) requires a bilty that documents the consignment details—vehicle description, origin, destination, and handling instructions. The bilty must be signed by the carrier, consignor, and the receiving agent. Ensure the bilty includes a unique tracking number and is stored electronically for audit purposes.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>One critical element that cannot be overlooked is the <strong>100% Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance</strong>. This policy guarantees that the full market value of the vehicle is insured against marine risks such as loss, damage, or theft during transit.</p>
<p>The insurer will provide a certificate that details the declared value, coverage limits, and the terms of indemnity. By opting for a 100% declared‑value policy, you eliminate the risk of under‑insurance, which could otherwise result in significant financial loss if an incident occurs.</p>

<p>In practice, these documents are compiled into a single transport packet. The packet is scanned and backed up digitally to maintain a record for both the carrier and the client.</p>
<p>When the vehicle arrives at the destination port, the packet is presented to customs officials, port authorities, and the receiving agent for verification. This systematic approach ensures compliance, protects the vehicle’s value, and facilitates a seamless handover at the final destination.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


